                <pb facs="0603" n="1563" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1563"/>

                <head>No. 1067.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Straus to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 27, 1888</date>.
                        (Received March 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 64.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The vice-consul-general has forwarded to me
                    a copy of a dispatch, No. 38, from Mr. Gillman, our consul at Jerusalem, to the
                    State Department, in relation to a suit at Jerusalem between a Turkish subject
                    and the cavass of the consulate, involving the dwelling-house wherein the said
                    cavass resided with his family and from which he was evicted.</p>
                <p>Having occasion to call upon the Grand Vizier on the 25th instant in relation to
                    other matters, I brought this complaint of Consul Gillman to his attention and
                    he appeared to be of the opinion that such cavass was entitled to the same
                    privileges as to domicile as are accorded to an American citizen, and he
                    immediately communicated with the governor of Jerusalem asking for explanation
                    for the course pursued.</p>
                <p>I trust by the time your instructions will have arrived the matter will have been
                    brought in this unofficial way to a satisfactory solution, and that my action
                    thus far will meet your approval.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O. S. Straus.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
